//# User-facing argv dispatch for `runtime/vibe`.
//#
//# Command parsing, diagnostic framing, path defaults, compile/check/fmt/
//# editor queries and host-action planning live here so the launcher is only
//# toolchain resolve + wasm invoke + host-only execution (run a guest,
//# wasmtime serve, minify, download/AOT).
//#
//# This file lives in the compiler package, next to cli_support.vibe, and not
//# in lib/@vibe/cli, because cli_adapter.vibe -- the committed seed's entry
//# and so the file every stage2.wasm is compiled from -- has to reach it: the
//# launcher hands its argv to whatever compiler wasm the toolchain installed,
//# and that is stage2. From lib/@vibe/cli this file would have to import this
//# package's facade for the ADR-0068 gates below, and cli_adapter.vibe is a
//# member of that facade, so `index.vpkg -> cli_adapter.vibe ->
//# cli/user_dispatch.vibe -> index.vpkg` is the same-node self-loop the
//# fs-mode cycle detector refuses (the `_cli_probe_entry.vibe` note in
//# index.vpkg records the first instance). lib/@vibe/cli/dispatch.vibe reaches
//# the dispatch entry points through the facade instead.

